  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: d4ecd1a615a340f4c9104ca01624d106, type: 3}
  m_Name: Loved
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Assembly-CSharp::YourCall.Dilemma
  _id: loved
  _verb: 0
  _weight: 2
  _narratorPrompt: Back to the very first lever. [amber]Five[/amber] strangers on the straight track. And on the branch, alone, [pink]the one you loved most[/pink] in all of it. Your partner. The person you would have grown old beside, if only you had kept off the wine and out of the car. [amber]Five over one[/amber], the sum unchanged since the first track. Everything else about it is not. Yes, I chose who stands there. Yes, on purpose. Your call.
  _choices:
  - _id: pull
    _label: Pull the lever
    _narratorReact: You pulled. You actually pulled. You took [pink]the one you loved most[/pink] and fed them to the wheels to spare five faces you had never seen and will never think of again. Oh, this one I am keeping. This is the reaction I will replay on the slow nights. The devoted partner, trading their beloved for a tidy little sum and a warm glow of arithmetic. I am not saying it was wrong. There is no wrong here, remember. I am only saying I have never enjoyed a pull quite this much.
    _narratorReactStruck:
    _struckParty: spur
    _gambledParty:
    _route: spur
    _diverts: 1
    _seedVotes: 52
    _endsGame: 0
    _profileImpact:
    - _axis: 0
      _value: 1
  - _id: do_nothing
    _label: Do nothing
    _narratorReact: You left it. Five strangers go under the wheels so [pink]the one you love[/pink] keeps breathing. On this exact rail, an hour ago, you pulled for strangers without a flicker. Turns out your precious arithmetic only ever balanced while the one on the short track was nobody to you. Predictable. Warm, even. And no comfort at all to the five.
    _narratorReactStruck:
    _struckParty: main
    _gambledParty:
    _route: straight
    _diverts: 0
    _seedVotes: 48
    _endsGame: 0
    _profileImpact:
    - _axis: 0
      _value: -1
